<article class="env-lemma" id="09ZB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09ZB">Lemma <span data-tag="09ZB">59.80.7</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a normal integral affine scheme with separably closed function field. Let $Z \subset X$ be a closed subscheme. For any finite abelian group $M$ we have $H^1_{\acute{e}tale}(Z, \underline{M}) = 0$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Cohomology on Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/03AJ" data-tag="03AJ">21.4.3</a> an element of $H^1_{\acute{e}tale}(Z, \underline{M})$ corresponds to a $\underline{M}$-torsor $\mathcal{F}$ on $Z_{\acute{e}tale}$. Such a torsor is clearly a finite locally constant sheaf. Hence $\mathcal{F}$ is representable by a scheme $V$ finite étale over $Z$, Lemma <a href="/tag/03RV" data-tag="03RV">59.64.4</a>. Of course $V \to Z$ is surjective as a torsor is locally trivial. Since $V \to Z$ has a section by Lemma <a href="/tag/09ZA" data-tag="09ZA">59.80.6</a> we are done. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>